@* Diff's Overview, written by hand after Code's and Collapsible's: two versions, side by side, every
   line, a diff computed first (TextDiff), the notes, then large texts (prose). Accessibility and See
   also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A diff shows the changes between two versions of a text, line by line, such as two versions of a config file. Removed and added lines carry a <Code>−</Code> or <Code>+</Code> and their old or new line number. The numbers and signs aren't copied when the user selects the lines.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>The diff is computed and colored on the server, so it looks the same <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">with JavaScript off</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Two versions</Heading>
<TextBlock>A diff compares an old and a new text, and folds the unchanged lines away from the changes. Set <Code>OldText</Code> and <Code>NewText</Code> to the two texts. To color them as code, set <Code>Language</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="diff-versions" />
<List>
    <ListItem>Each text is colored whole before it's split into lines, so a comment or value across several lines keeps its color.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>In a removed line beside an added one, the changed words are marked, unless less than half of the longer line is unchanged. To turn this off, set <Code>MarkWords="false"</Code>.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Code>Context</Code> sets how many unchanged lines stay beside each change (3 by default). The rest fold into a row that the user clicks to show them in place.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Side by side</Heading>
<TextBlock>A split diff shows the old text beside the new, with each removed line beside the line it became. It suits wide screens. Set <Code>Layout="DiffLayout.Split"</Code> to turn it on.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="diff-side-by-side" />
<TextBlock>Below 45rem wide, a split diff shows as unified. Long lines wrap rather than scroll. Unchanged lines appear on both sides, so a split diff sends them twice.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Showing unchanged lines</Heading>
<TextBlock>For a short text, a diff can show every line, with no folding. Set <Code>Fold="false"</Code> to show every unchanged line. To leave the line numbers out, set <Code>LineNumbers="false"</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="diff-every-line" />

<Heading Level="2">A diff computed first</Heading>
<TextBlock>You can compute the diff yourself and pass the lines to the component, such as to count the changes first. Compute it with <Code>TextDiff.Compare</Code> or elsewhere, and set <Code>Lines</Code> to the result.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="diff-computed" />
<List>
    <ListItem><Code>TextDiff.Compare(oldText, newText)</Code> returns every line of both texts as a <Code>DiffLine</Code>, with its <Code>Kind</Code>, <Code>OldNumber</Code>, <Code>NewNumber</Code> and <Code>Text</Code>.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>It returns null when the texts differ by more lines than it looks for.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>Lines from elsewhere must be every line of both texts, in order, with removed lines before the added lines that replace them.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">No changes, or too many</Heading>
<TextBlock>The diff shows a note when the texts are the same, or when they differ by more than <Code>MaxChanges</Code> lines. To change the notes, set <Code>SameText</Code> and <Code>TooManyText</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="diff-notes" />

<Heading Level="2">Large texts</Heading>
<TextBlock>A diff compares at most <Code>MaxChanges</Code> removed and added lines (1,000 by default); past that, it shows the too-many note. Folded lines are still in the page, ready to open, so a 5,000-line file with one change sends 5,000 lines. To keep a long diff in a scrolling box, set <Code>MaxHeight</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Diff OldText="@older.Xml" NewText="@newer.Xml" Language="xml" Title="v3 → v4" />

        <Diff OldText="@before" NewText="@after" Language="csharp" Layout="DiffLayout.Split" />
        """;
}
